Net options through the UI (server team).",[210,217,218,219],{},"For superusers:\n",[207,220,221,228,234,240],{},[210,222,223,227],{},[224,225,226],"strong",{},"Limiter",": Define which permissions each faction can assign to roles.",[210,229,230,233],{},[224,231,232],{},"Laws",": Configure law entries for each faction.",[210,235,236,239],{},[224,237,238],{},"Filestore",": Configure file storage per faction.",[210,241,242,245],{},[224,243,244],{},"App config",": Configure options that affect the entire FiveNet instance.",[202,247,249],{"id":248},"role-management","Role Management",[191,251,252],{},"Factions can manage their own roles when this is allowed by the permission system.",[191,254,255],{},[194,256],{"alt":257,"src":258},"features-settings-roles.webp","\u002Fimages\u002Fscreenshots\u002Ffeatures-settings-roles.webp",[202,260,262],{"id":261},"limiter-and-roles-explained","Limiter And Roles Explained",[191,264,265],{},"To allow role self-service safely, use the limiter to define the maximum permission set a faction can assign.\nFor example, you can allow the police faction to see colleague positions on the livemap, while preventing unauthorized factions from assigning that permission.\nIn practice, the limiter is a list of permissions and attributes available to roles within a faction.",[191,267,268],{},"Usually, the server management team defines these limits for each faction.",[202,270,272],{"id":271},"discord-bot-sync-roles-to-your-factions-discord","Discord Bot - Sync roles to your faction's Discord",[191,274,275],{},"Sync examples:",[207,277,278,281,284],{},[210,279,280],{},"Employee ranks",[210,282,283],{},"Absent\u002Fvacation status",[210,285,286,287,291],{},"Server-team groups on Discord servers connected to FiveNet (for example a ",[288,289,290],"code",{},"Project Leader"," role)",[191,293,294],{},[194,295],{"alt":296,"src":297},"Feature Settings - Job Props - Discord Bot","\u002Fimages\u002Fscreenshots\u002Ffeatures-discordbot.webp",[202,299,301],{"id":300},"app-config","App Config",[191,303,304],{},[194,305],{"alt":306,"src":307},"Feature Settings - App Config","\u002Fimages\u002Fscreenshots\u002Ffeatures-settings-appconfig.webp",[191,309,310],{},"App config contains options that affect the whole FiveNet instance, including:",[207,312,313,316,319,322,325,328],{},[210,314,315],{},"The default language for the app.",[210,317,318],{},"Default permissions.",[210,320,321],{},"Imprint and Privacy Policy links.",[210,323,324],{},"Livemap sync intervals.",[210,326,327],{},"Banner message with expiration time (for example to announce maintenance).",[210,329,330],{},"And more.",{"title":332,"searchDepth":333,"depth":333,"links":334},"",2,[335,336,337,338,339],{"id":204,"depth":333,"text":205},{"id":248,"depth":333,"text":249},{"id":261,"depth":333,"text":262},{"id":271,"depth":333,"text":272},{"id":300,"depth":333,"text":301},"Learn how to configure and manage settings in FiveNet, including job properties, roles, permissions, and app-wide configurations.","md",null,{},true,"\u002Fuser-guides\u002Fsettings",{"title":186,"description":340},"3.user-guides\u002F7.settings","55vLMLgIY1GeHaFsgf81izPAfEv7G1PM8n8Tr8OtcYE",[350,353],{"title":146,"path":351,"stem":352,"description":332,"children":-1},"\u002Fuser-guides\u002Fmailer","3.user-guides\u002F6.mailer",{"title":354,"path":355,"stem":356,"description":357,"children":-1},"Languages (i18n)","\u002Fuser-guides\u002Fi18n","3.user-guides\u002F8.i18n","FiveNet supports multiple languages.",1788932298646]